# Game project

This is a SvelteKit game. Game logic lives in `src/lib/` with **registry + definition + factory** patterns.

## Required reading

Before changing `src/lib/` or `tests/`, read [agents/README.md](../../agents/README.md) and follow [agents/guidelines/](../../agents/guidelines/).

## Skills

| Task | Skill |
|------|--------|
| New/changed definitions, index, types | `game-data-registry` (`.cursor/skills/data-registry/`) |
| Tests for registries/factories | `game-registry-tests` (`.cursor/skills/registry-tests/`) |

## Hard rules

- Never use nested ternary operators — use `if/else` or a helper ([agents/guidelines/05-code-style.md](../../agents/guidelines/05-code-style.md)).
- Tests mirror `src/lib/` under `tests/` — no per-entity definition test files.
- Registry keys must equal `definition.id`.
- Factories validate with `id in REGISTRY`, never `switch` + `Object.keys().includes()`.
- Shared JSDoc types in domain `types.js`, derived from `index.js`.

Reference: `src/lib/items/weapons/` and `tests/lib/items/weapons/`.
